    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0193" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg871"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Clay.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 6, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of May 7 (No. 3) has been
                    submitted to the President, and is approved. The speech which you addressed to
                    his Imperial Majesty truthfully made known the sentiments of this government
                    towards Russia, and it has received with much satisfaction the renewed
                    assurances of friendship and good will which the Emperor gave you on the
                    occasion of your presentation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius</hi> M. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Clay</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
